  "classification": "known_family",
  "attribution_confidence": "high",
  "description": "Lumma C2 (LummaC2) logs. The panel writes `System.txt` with a\nYAML-like dash-prefix list (`- LummaC2 Build:`,\n`- Configuration:`, etc.) and a distinctive `(sig:UNIX.HEX)`\nsignature on the `Time:` line. Build banners reference the\n`@lummanowork` channel; the panel is sold MaaS via\n`@lummamarketplace_bot`.",
  "aliases": [
    "LummaC2",
    "Lumma Stealer"
  ],
  "typical_targets": [
    "Browser saved credentials, cookies, autofill",
    "Crypto wallet extensions (focus on MetaMask, Phantom, and similar)",
    "Steam, Telegram, Discord session tokens",
    "2FA seeds from Authy and similar desktop clients",
    "Cryptocurrency seed phrases harvested from text files"
  ],
  "detection_notes": "High-confidence trigger: the `(sig:UNIX.HEX)` parenthesised\nsignature on the `- Time:` line. Together with the\n`- LummaC2 Build:` banner this is unambiguous Lumma. Several\nderivative families (Remus, AL Stealer, BabaStealer,\nArtHouseCloud, CashFlow) share the dash-prefix shape but lack\nthe signature; they should be tracked separately.",
